    {
      "index": 17,
      "section": "Section 5 \u2014 Patch Walkthrough",
      "slide_id": "05c-modulator-b",
      "heading": "Step 3: Modulator B at \u221a2 ratio",
      "cue_id": "op-poly-bell-step3",
      "kind": "operator-demo",
      "narration_before": "onds, sustain at minus infinity, release eighty milliseconds. The modulator's envelope is shorter than the carrier's \u2014 bright initial transient, then the spectrum fades back toward sine. Listen. That metallic shimmer in the attack \u2014 that's the Bessel sidebands at an irrational ratio, decaying with the modulator's level envelope. Same engineering trick James used on every bell tone across *Drukqs*.",
