    {
      "index": 19,
      "section": "Section 5 \u2014 Patch Walkthrough",
      "slide_id": "05e-feedback",
      "heading": "Step 5: Feedback on C",
      "cue_id": "op-poly-bell-step5",
      "kind": "operator-demo",
      "narration_before": " top of the algorithm-one stack \u2014 feedback is enabled there. At thirty percent the operator self-modulates lightly. The waveform leans away from sine toward a slightly skewed shape, and a bit of grit lands in the attack transient. Listen. That grit is what keeps the patch from sounding like a clean Eno bell. The whole point of high-feedback FM is the texture \u2014 and we only need a little of it here.",
