    {
      "index": 21,
      "section": "Section 5 \u2014 Patch Walkthrough",
      "slide_id": "05g-velocity",
      "heading": "Step 7: Velocity Routing",
      "cue_id": "op-poly-bell-step7",
      "kind": "operator-demo",
      "narration_before": "nce between a static patch and a playable one. On operator B, set Time-less-than-Vel to plus thirty. That means harder velocities shorten the modulator envelope \u2014 the bell rings shorter and brighter when struck hard. Then set Level-less-than-Vel to plus fifty. Harder velocities increase the modulator level \u2014 meaning the modulation index \u2014 meaning the brightness. Listen. Soft note first. Then hard.",
