    {
      "index": 25,
      "section": "Section 6 \u2014 IDM Application",
      "slide_id": "06a-rhythmic-fm",
      "heading": "Rhythmic FM via Loop Modes",
      "cue_id": "op-rhythmic-single",
      "kind": "operator-demo",
      "narration_before": " \u2014 opens with exactly this. Metallic clicks, each one a short modulator envelope ringing a carrier at a ratio that lands on no musical interval. Percussion with pitch character but no pitch identity. Booth said in the WATMM AMA that *Incunabula* is full of FM synths \u2014 they liked them precisely because they do not behave like analog filters. Hit them harder and they get more inharmonic, not warmer.",
