    },
    {
      "index": 26,
      "section": "Section 6 \u2014 IDM Application",
      "slide_id": "06b-layer",
      "heading": "Layered Polyrhythm",
      "cue_id": "op-rhythmic-layered",
      "kind": "operator-demo",
      "narration_before": "aking melodies and started making textures. Sean Booth, in the watmm AMA in twenty-thirteen: *\"the line between sequencing and synthesis is pretty much gone now. textures are sequences, sequences are like harmonies. it's all the same thing when you get down to it.\"* Once your synth *is* the rhythm, the line dissolves. Operator's loop modes are the cheapest way to get there in any contemporary DAW.",
